first Republicans in Congress are  demanding an investigation into  Christopher Steele he's the author of  the infamous Trump dossier that has  dominated politics in this country for  an entire year  fox chief intelligence correspondent  catherine herridge is all over this  story and she joins us tonight  well Thank You Tucker this case matters  because it's the first known criminal  referral from Congress as part of the  Russia investigations the Republican  chairman of the Senate Judiciary  Committee chuck Grassley who was  oversight for the FBI and Justice  Department along with his Senate  colleague Senator Lindsey Graham believe  there is a violation of 18 USC which is  lying to federal authorities commonly  known as the Martha Stewart statute  according to the letter made public  today the senators believe potential  violations for false statements relate  to Christopher Steele's distribution of  the unverified Trump dossier a  half-dozen major media outlets were  briefed before the election Steele was  on the payroll of opposition research  firm fusion GPS whose co-founder is  former journalist Glenn Simpson in the  months leading up to the election  Simpson told steel to brief reporters at  least twice after no reporters ran with  the story the project was of course  funded by the DNC and Clinton campaign  senator Grassley said the criminal  referral is about a perceived double  standard Trump campaign associates were  prosecuted for lying to the FBI and the  same standard should apply to others  regardless of politics tonight a senior  Senate Democrat Richard Blumenthal  called the referral partisan and said  the Russian investigation was triggered  by information entirely separate from  the dossier car catherine herridge  thank you very much for that
 

